--TEST--
Tokenizer input larger than PHL_MAX_INPUT cap is rejected with a compile error
--DESCRIPTION--
Run under a small per-input cap (PHL_MAX_INPUT=32768, set by `make test-stress`).
The script body is padded past 32768 bytes so ph7_compile() rejects it before
tokenizing any input, and "UNREACHABLE" is never printed.
--SKIPIF--
<?php if (!getenv('PHL_MAX_INPUT')) { echo "skip needs PHL_MAX_INPUT cap (run: make test-stress)"; } ?>
